From: Anton Alexander <anton@antonai-work>
Date: 2026-05-06
Subject: [PATCH] topo: raise NCCL_TOPO_XML_MAX_NODES from 256 to 2048

The DeepEP V2 cross-node dispatch on p5.48xlarge (H100 x 8, EFA x 32)
hits the 256-node fuse ceiling in ncclTopoFuseXml during intra-node
graph construction. Per-rank autogen XML contains rank-specific attrs
(rank, pci_busid) that defeat the attribute-equality check in
ncclTopoFuseXmlRecursive, so 8 ranks x ~125 nodes > 256.

Neither NCCL_TOPO_FILE override nor FI_EFA_DEVICE_LIST mitigate the
overflow. The only fix is to raise the cap. 2048 covers 8 ranks at
~250 nodes each with headroom.

---
 src/graph/topo.h | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/graph/topo.h b/src/graph/topo.h
index abcdef0..1234567 100644
--- a/src/graph/topo.h
+++ b/src/graph/topo.h
@@ -189,7 +189,7 @@
 #define NCCL_TOPO_ID_SYSTEM_ID(id) (id >> 56)
 #define NCCL_TOPO_ID_LOCAL_ID(id) (id & 0x00ffffffffffffff)
 #define NCCL_TOPO_ID(systemId, localId) (((int64_t)systemId << 56) + (localId & 0x00ffffffffffffff))
-#define NCCL_TOPO_XML_MAX_NODES 256
+#define NCCL_TOPO_XML_MAX_NODES 2048

 // Map between CPU affinity domain and PCI bus ID (IOMMU or ACPI namespace)

--
